-- `@inline(always)` on a body that calls itself - back from `Reject.Inline.Legacy.yana`.
--
-- # resolver: ownership
--
-- A body that calls itself is the one shape of `@inline(always)` that is still an error, and it is
-- the only one: every copy of it contains the same call, so there is no number of expansions after
-- which the attribute has been carried out. Refused once, at the declaration. It was left to the
-- graft's depth limit, which met it eight copies deep in every function that called it and in the
-- body's own conversion, and followed each with two internal errors about the missing result.
-- A branch or a call to something *else* is admitted and taken by the inliner - see
-- AlwaysInline.Branch.yana, which is where those live.

@inline(always)
fn countingDown(x: Int) -> Int = if x <= 0 then 0 else countingDown(x - 1) + 1

fn main() -> Int = countingDown(6)
